[0;36m[LOW][0m [1;37mScreenshots and task snapshots allowed[0m  (MAVS-MANIFEST-SNAPSHOT)
    No FLAG_SECURE and no excludeFromRecents were found, so the OS may capture snapshots of sensitive screens for the recents view.
    CWE-200 | MASVS-PLATFORM-3
    [4;37mEvidence:[0m
      - FLAG_SECURE / excludeFromRecents not detected
    [4;37mVerify:[0m Background the app on a sensitive screen and inspect the snapshot.
    [1;33m[+] Exploit:[0m
      Note: root access required to access snapshots.
      Open the application to a screen with sensitive info, then switch to another app or the homescreen. A snapshot will have been created. Verify the image is not blank by accessing it:
      adb shell "su -c 'cp -r /data/system/recent_images /sdcard/'"
      adb pull /sdcard/recent_images
      adb shell "su -c 'rm -r /sdcard/recent_images'"
        or
      adb shell "su -c 'cp -r /data/system_ce/0/snapshots /sdcard/'"
      adb pull /sdcard/snapshots
      adb shell "su -c 'rm -r /sdcard/snapshots'"
      Newer versions of Android:
      adb shell "su -c 'cp -rf /data/system_ce/0/snapshots /data/local/tmp/'"
      chmod -R 777 "/data/local/tmp/snapshots"
      adb pull "/data/local/tmp/snapshots"
      adb shell "su -c 'rm -r /data/local/tmp/snapshots'"

